<p>Recently in development, when integrating third-party projects into my project using CocoaPods, I keep forgetting how to link third-party libraries and how to write podspec. So I’m recording this easily forgotten content.</p>

<h2 id="creating-a-podspec">Creating a podspec</h2>

<p>In the test project directory, create a directory called demoframeworks, then run the following inside it:</p>

<div class="language-sh highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
</pre></td><td class="rouge-code"><pre>pod spec create spec名称
</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>
<blockquote>
  <p>Give the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">spec</code> a name of your own.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>A spec template will be generated locally.
Then edit the spec file with a text editor. Here we’ll use Agora’s SDK as an example.</p>

