<p>Then add this to the Podfile content:</p>

<div class="language-sh highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
2
3
4
5
6
7
</pre></td><td class="rouge-code"><pre>target <span class="s1">'PodSpecDemo'</span> <span class="k">do</span>
  <span class="c"># Comment the next line if you don't want to use dynamic frameworks</span>
  use_frameworks!

  <span class="c"># Add this line</span>
  pod <span class="s1">'specdemo'</span>, :path<span class="o">=&gt;</span><span class="s1">'./demoframeworks'</span>
end
</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>

<p>Note: <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">specdemo</code> here is the name we give the local pod being integrated; it’s best to keep it consistent with the name of the created spec.</p>

<p>Then run pod install.</p>

<p>Finally the project becomes exactly what we want.</p>

